    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/06/new-balance-fuelcell-supercomp-elite-v5.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The FuelCell (PEBA) midsole is comfortable with a soft/compressive heel for impact protection, then transitions into a firmer, stiffer forefoot feel.",
        "Responsiveness: It feels somewhat snappier than prior versions but is not especially bouncy or highly propulsive, performing better at tempo/marathon paces than top-end speed.",
        "Stability: Torsional/longitudinal rigidity is high (very stiff plate, minimal flexibility), lockdown is secure, but the narrower platform and semi-rigid/flexible heel counter make it less forgiving laterally than earlier SC Elite models.",
        "Durability: Overall durability is rated as average; wet-road outsole traction is noted as good, with no standout evidence of exceptional long-term outsole or upper longevity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/06/new-balance-fuelcell-sc-elite-v5-multi.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning is moderately firm but deeply protective (40 mm heel / 32 mm forefoot), with a cushioned, secure heel feel and a firmer, flatter forefoot transition.",
        "Responsiveness is a weakness: testers report limited bounce/energy return, a flat ride, and less snap at faster efforts due to rigid midfoot-to-toe-off behavior.",
        "Stability is a major strength: despite a much narrower heel/midfoot platform, rearfoot stability is rated among the best in super shoes, supported by a firm high heel counter and medial support geometry.",
        "Durability signals are positive from deep heel rubber and broad forefoot rubber coverage plus good grip (even on gravel), though some forefoot rubber may add weight without clear ground-contact benefit."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/new-balance-sc-elite-v5-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Ride is slightly firmer and less squishy than v4, but still soft/forgiving enough for long efforts; heel-to-forefoot protection stayed comfortable through marathon distance despite reduced foam volume.",
        "Responsiveness: Updated forefoot plate tuning with PEBA FuelCell adds clear pop, bounce, and sharper/snappier toe-offs, giving a more race-ready feel.",
        "Stability: Forefoot rigidity is higher from the stiffer plate, but the platform is narrower (about 25% slimmer) with lower forefoot stack, so lateral support may feel less accommodating for some runners; heel hold improved via a cushier heel counter and secure upper.",
        "Durability: Early signs are strong, with reviewers saying the shoe held up well across training and a marathon; updated forefoot/outsole rubber plus a solid single-layer mesh upper indicate improved wear longevity and grip."
      ]
    }
  ],
